<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">encumbrance</ansi>

There is one carrying limit, and it belongs to the whole company: the
weight everyone carries, wears, and keeps in the cargo, against what the
members, their packs, and their horses can bear
(<ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>). How many items you hold doesn't matter, only how
much they weigh.

Once the company is full, no one can pick up, buy, or be handed
anything more. A heavy load slows journeys and makes walking more
tiring (<ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>), but walking is never blocked.

In a fight, only your own worn and carried weight counts, against your
Strength: a heavy personal load cuts your dodge, and the company's
packs, horses, and cargo never lighten it (<ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company inventory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help mount</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>.
